---
import '../styles/studio.css';
const examples = [
  { id: 'pixel-loot', title: 'Tiny loot icon', subject: 'a red mushroom with white spots', note: 'One object, a simple silhouette and a small palette. A good starting point for inventory icons.' },
  { id: 'pixel-character', title: 'Adventure character', subject: 'a small red-haired forest ranger in a green cloak holding a wooden staff', note: 'One complete character with a readable pose. Try changing the clothing or profession first.' },
  { id: 'pixel-isometric', title: 'Isometric hideaway', subject: 'a tiny timber cabin with a red roof and a glowing round window', note: 'One building on a small ground tile. Keep the perspective and light direction consistent.' },
  { id: 'pixel-landscape', title: 'Scenic world', subject: 'a quiet mountain lake with a small wooden cabin and tall pine trees', note: 'Foreground, focal point and distant scenery. A wide aspect ratio also works.' },
];
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><meta name="description" content="FLUX.2-klein Pixel Art recipes and practical tips for Atelier."/><title>Pixel Art — Atelier Guide</title></head><body>
<header><a class="brand" href="/studio/">← atelier</a><span>Pixel art guide · November 4, 2026</span></header>
<main style="max-width:1100px;padding-bottom:70px"><section class="intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">SMALL GRIDS. CLEAR IDEAS.</p><h1>Build a little world.</h1><p>Choose FLUX.2-klein · Pixel Art, pick a recipe and describe your subject. The PXART4 LoRA produces a clean pixel grid at 1024 square. All components are Apache-2.0.</p><a class="quiet button" href="/studio/#explore">Choose an example ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="guide"><div><h2>Start here</h2><p>Use the recipe’s Recommended settings: 1024 × 1024, 20 Euler steps, CFG 4. Change the subject first. Keep a fixed seed while comparing a pose, color or palette.</p><p>The PXART4 LoRA is trained on a free-to-use pixel art dataset and produces a clean pixel grid without a separate cleanup step. The base model is FLUX.2-klein-4B (Apache-2.0); the LoRA is also Apache-2.0.</p></div><div><h3>Choose the right recipe</h3><p><strong>Loot icon:</strong> one object, a simple silhouette and a small palette.<br/><strong>Character:</strong> one complete character with a readable pose.<br/><strong>Isometric:</strong> one building on a small ground tile.<br/><strong>Landscape:</strong> foreground, focal point and distant scenery.</p></div></section>
<section aria-labelledby="examples-title"><h2 id="examples-title">Generated here, ready to try</h2><p>These examples use the installed model and the same presets available under Explore. “Use this example” in the studio restores the recorded inputs and seed.</p><div class="recipe-grid">{examples.map(example => <article class="recipe-card"><img src={'/studio/recipe-examples/'+example.id+'.webp'} width="1024" height="1024" loading="lazy" alt={example.subject}/><div class="recipe-card-body"><h3>{example.title}</h3><p>{example.note}</p><p><strong>Subject:</strong> {example.subject}</p></div></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="guide"><div><h2>Know the limits</h2><p>The LoRA produces a clean pixel grid, but it does not guarantee tileable textures, coherent animation frames or correct anatomy. Check the actual drawing, outlines and perspective yourself. The background stays opaque; use a contrasting background and a pixel editor when preparing sprites for a game.</p></div><div><h2>Model and sources</h2><p><a href="https://huggingface.co/adirik/pixel-art-lora-flux.2-klein-4B" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">adirik · Pixel Art LoRA for FLUX.2-klein-4B ↗</a></p><p><a href="https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-4B" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Black Forest Labs · FLUX.2-klein-4B ↗</a></p><p><a href="https://huggingface.co/leejet/FLUX.2-klein-4B-GGUF" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">leejet · FLUX.2-klein-4B GGUF ↗</a></p><p>All components are Apache-2.0. The application adds no content filter.</p></div></section>
</main></body></html>
